# The tick sends at most 16 MIDI packets a ms (the device's USB-MIDI out ring holds 64 and drops what does not fit,
# with no way to ask for room): a burst waits its turn in the queue, in order, and the registry counts a note as
# sounding only once its note-on has gone out. The burst: 64 note-ons on channel 16 (15 on the wire), due now, and
# their offs a tick later, put in the queue of the playing Full ensemble.
dumpmidi app/build/scenarios/send_rate/dump.txt
tap PLAY
wait 500
rt burst 64
wait 1
expect sounding15 <17
expect per_ms 16
wait 1
expect sounding15 <33
wait 20
expect sounding15 0
expect per_ms 16
dumpcount 9F 00 01
expect dumpcount 1
dumpcount 9F 3F 01
expect dumpcount 1
dumpcount 8F 3F 00
expect dumpcount 1
expect dropped 0
